"158":{"id":"/docs/components/calendar-27","page_id":"/docs/components/calendar","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/calendar#min--max","content":"Bounding selectable dates."},"159":{"id":"/docs/components/calendar-28","page_id":"/docs/components/calendar","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/calendar#unavailable","content":"Disabling scattered individual dates with `isDateUnavailable`."},"160":{"id":"/docs/components/calendar-29","page_id":"/docs/components/calendar","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/calendar#disabled","content":"A fully disabled calendar."},"161":{"id":"/docs/components/calendar-30","page_id":"/docs/components/calendar","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/calendar#accessibility","content":"Arrow keys move by day; PageUp/PageDown by month; Home/End to row edges"},"162":{"id":"/docs/components/calendar-31","page_id":"/docs/components/calendar","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/calendar#accessibility","content":"Focus-visible outline; disabled days are not focusable"},"163":{"id":"/docs/components/calendar-32","page_id":"/docs/components/calendar","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/calendar#accessibility","content":"Out-of-month days render at reduced opacity and are not selectable"},"164":{"id":"/docs/components/calendar-33","page_id":"/docs/components/calendar","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/calendar#best-practices","content":"Always provide an `aria-label` on standalone calendars."},"165":{"id":"/docs/components/calendar-34","page_id":"/docs/components/calendar","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/calendar#best-practices","content":"Use `isDateUnavailable` for scattered disabled days; use `minValue` / `maxValue` for contiguous bounds."},"166":{"id":"/docs/components/calendar-35","page_id":"/docs/components/calendar","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/calendar#troubleshooting","content":"Dates not formatting per locale? Ensure the app is wrapped in `<I18nProvider locale=\"…\">`."},"167":{"id":"/docs/components/carousel","page_id":"/docs/components/carousel","type":"page","content":"Carousel","breadcrumbs":["Docs","Components"],"tags":[],"url":"/docs/components/carousel"},"168":{"id":"/docs/components/carousel-0","page_id":"/docs/components/carousel","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/carousel","content":"The Carousel component allows users to cycle through a series of content panels (typically images, cards, or text) in a horizontal or vertical layout. It is commonly used for featured content, product showcases, or testimonials."},"169":{"id":"/docs/components/carousel-1","page_id":"/docs/components/carousel","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/components/carousel#installation","content":"Installation"},"170":{"id":"/docs/components/carousel-2","page_id":"/docs/components/carousel","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/components/carousel#examples","content":"Examples"},"171":{"id":"/docs/components/carousel-3","page_id":"/docs/components/carousel","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/components/carousel#default","content":"Default"},"172":{"id":"/docs/components/carousel-4","page_id":"/docs/components/carousel","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/components/carousel#controlled","content":"Controlled"},"173":{"id":"/docs/components/carousel-5","page_id":"/docs/components/carousel","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/components/carousel#external-controls-uncontrolled","content":"External Controls (Uncontrolled)"},"174":{"id":"/docs/components/carousel-6","page_id":"/docs/components/carousel","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/components/carousel#external-controls-controlled","content":"External Controls (Controlled)"},"175":{"id":"/docs/components/carousel-7","page_id":"/docs/components/carousel","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/components/carousel#hide-controls","content":"Hide Controls"},"176":{"id":"/docs/components/carousel-8","page_id":"/docs/components/carousel","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/components/carousel#variable-widths","content":"Variable Widths"},"177":{"id":"/docs/components/carousel-9","page_id":"/docs/components/carousel","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/components/carousel#events","content":"Events"},"178":{"id":"/docs/components/carousel-10","page_id":"/docs/components/carousel","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/components/carousel#rtl-direction","content":"RTL Direction"},"179":{"id":"/docs/components/carousel-11","page_id":"/docs/components/carousel","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/components/carousel#props","content":"Props"},"180":{"id":"/docs/components/carousel-12","page_id":"/docs/components/carousel","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/components/carousel#carousel","content":"Carousel"},"181":{"id":"/docs/components/carousel-13","page_id":"/docs/components/carousel","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/carousel#default","content":"The default carousel is a carousel that is uncontrolled, it shows the first slide by default. You can also pass the `defaultActiveIndex` prop to the `Carousel` component to set the initial active slide index."},"182":{"id":"/docs/components/carousel-14","page_id":"/docs/components/carousel","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/carousel#controlled","content":"The controlled carousel is a carousel that is controlled by the `activeIndex` prop."},"183":{"id":"/docs/components/carousel-15","page_id":"/docs/components/carousel","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/carousel#external-controls-uncontrolled","content":"You can control the carousel externally by passing the `ref` prop to the `Carousel` component and using the `emblaApi` to control the carousel imperatively."},"184":{"id":"/docs/components/carousel-16","page_id":"/docs/components/carousel","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/carousel#external-controls-controlled","content":"You can control the carousel externally by using the `activeIndex` prop to control the active slide index."},"185":{"id":"/docs/components/carousel-17","page_id":"/docs/components/carousel","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/carousel#hide-controls","content":"The hide controls carousel is a carousel that hides the navigation controls."},"186":{"id":"/docs/components/carousel-18","page_id":"/docs/components/carousel","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/carousel#variable-widths","content":"It supports multiple slides with different widths."},"187":{"id":"/docs/components/carousel-19","page_id":"/docs/components/carousel","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/carousel#events","content":"You can listen to events like `onChange`, `onPrev`, or `onNext`."},"188":{"id":"/docs/components/carousel-20","page_id":"/docs/components/carousel","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/carousel#rtl-direction","content":"The carousel follows the current **layout direction** (LTR or RTL). By default, that direction is detected automatically from the browser or system settings."},"189":{"id":"/docs/components/card","page_id":"/docs/components/card","type":"page","content":"Card","breadcrumbs":["Docs","Components"],"tags":[],"url":"/docs/components/card"},"190":{"id":"/docs/components/card-0","page_id":"/docs/components/card","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/card","content":"A surface that groups related content and actions."},"191":{"id":"/docs/components/card-1","page_id":"/docs/components/card","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/components/card#installation","content":"Installation"},"192":{"id":"/docs/components/card-2","page_id":"/docs/components/card","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/components/card#examples","content":"Examples"},"193":{"id":"/docs/components/card-3","page_id":"/docs/components/card","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/components/card#default","content":"Default"},"194":{"id":"/docs/components/card-4","page_id":"/docs/components/card","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/components/card#text-lockup","content":"Text lockup"},"195":{"id":"/docs/components/card-5","page_id":"/docs/components/card","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/components/card#corner-actions","content":"Corner actions"},"196":{"id":"/docs/components/card-6","page_id":"/docs/components/card","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/components/card#link","content":"Link"},"197":{"id":"/docs/components/card-7","page_id":"/docs/components/card","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/components/card#media","content":"Media"},"198":{"id":"/docs/components/card-8","page_id":"/docs/components/card","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/components/card#actions","content":"Actions"},"199":{"id":"/docs/components/card-9","page_id":"/docs/components/card","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/components/card#checkbox","content":"Checkbox"},"200":{"id":"/docs/components/card-10","page_id":"/docs/components/card","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/components/card#radio","content":"Radio"},"201":{"id":"/docs/components/card-11","page_id":"/docs/components/card","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/components/card#disabled","content":"Disabled"},"202":{"id":"/docs/components/card-12","page_id":"/docs/components/card","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/components/card#layout","content":"Layout"},"203":{"id":"/docs/components/card-13","page_id":"/docs/components/card","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/components/card#customization","content":"Customization"},"204":{"id":"/docs/components/card-14","page_id":"/docs/components/card","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/components/card#accessibility","content":"Accessibility"},"205":{"id":"/docs/components/card-15","page_id":"/docs/components/card","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/components/card#props","content":"Props"},"206":{"id":"/docs/components/card-16","page_id":"/docs/components/card","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/components/card#card","content":"Card"},"207":{"id":"/docs/components/card-17","page_id":"/docs/components/card","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/components/card#cardselectionindicator","content":"CardSelectionIndicator"},"208":{"id":"/docs/components/card-18","page_id":"/docs/components/card","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/card","content":"Card groups related content, like media, text, and actions, on a single surface. It can also\nwork as a link or button, or be selected like a checkbox or radio, but not both."},"209":{"id":"/docs/components/card-19","page_id":"/docs/components/card","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/card#default","content":"A static Card just renders its children."},"210":{"id":"/docs/components/card-20","page_id":"/docs/components/card","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/card#text-lockup","content":"Compose Card with TextLockup for eyebrow, title, and body."},"211":{"id":"/docs/components/card-21","page_id":"/docs/components/card","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/card#corner-actions","content":"Direct CornerActions sit at the top-end of the Card."},"212":{"id":"/docs/components/card-22","page_id":"/docs/components/card","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/card#link","content":"`href` renders the Card itself as a native link, so layered content like an elevated Box stays\nclickable. The link takes its name from its content unless you pass `aria-label`. Do not nest\ncontrols in a link Card."},"213":{"id":"/docs/components/card-23","page_id":"/docs/components/card","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/card#media","content":"Use default padding for inset media, or zero Card padding with a padded lockup for full bleed.\nMedia can stand alone, follow the text, or be a custom Box. Clip only the media region."},"214":{"id":"/docs/components/card-24","page_id":"/docs/components/card","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/card#actions","content":"`onPress` is the Card primary. Nested buttons keep their own hits, so Save does not open the\nModal. Compose a Card inside the Modal when the action is a focused form."},"215":{"id":"/docs/components/card-25","page_id":"/docs/components/card","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/card#checkbox","content":"Standalone checkbox Cards own their state. Grouped cards belong in CheckboxGroup.\nIndicator children can render custom content from the current selection state."},"216":{"id":"/docs/components/card-26","page_id":"/docs/components/card","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/card#radio","content":"Radio Cards require a value and live in RadioGroup, which owns selection and arrow-key movement."},"217":{"id":"/docs/components/card-27","page_id":"/docs/components/card","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/card#disabled","content":"`isDisabled` disables the Card's primary action or selection and fades the whole Card. A\ndisabled CheckboxGroup or RadioGroup does the same. Read-only selection keeps its value visible."},"218":{"id":"/docs/components/card-28","page_id":"/docs/components/card","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/card#layout","content":"Use Grid for responsiveness."},"219":{"id":"/docs/components/card-29","page_id":"/docs/components/card","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/card#customization","content":"`CardSelectionIndicator` only shows the selection state. The Card owns the native checkbox or\nradio, so a selection Card keeps its keyboard stop and form value without an indicator. Pass\nnon-interactive children or a selection-state render function to replace the default circle and\nicon. See the Checkbox example."},"220":{"id":"/docs/components/card-30","page_id":"/docs/components/card","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/card#customization","content":"To style the Card by state, target `[data-card-selected]` and `[data-disabled]` from your\n`className`."},"221":{"id":"/docs/components/card-31","page_id":"/docs/components/card","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/card#accessibility","content":"Name an `onPress` action or selection with `aria-label` or `aria-labelledby`. The stretched\ncontrol and the selection input have no visible label of their own."},"222":{"id":"/docs/components/card-32","page_id":"/docs/components/card","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/card#accessibility","content":"On a Card without a primary action or selection, `aria-label`, `aria-labelledby`, and\n`aria-describedby` apply to the surface, for example with `role=\"region\"`."},"223":{"id":"/docs/components/card-33","page_id":"/docs/components/card","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/card#accessibility","content":"`href` renders the Card itself as a native link, named by its content unless you pass\n`aria-label`. A link Card cannot contain controls, so do not put CornerActions, buttons,\ninputs, or selection in an `href` Card. Clicking body text on an `onPress` or\nselection Card activates it; dragging that text selects it."},"224":{"id":"/docs/components/card-34","page_id":"/docs/components/card","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/card#accessibility","content":"`isDisabled` disables the primary action or selection and fades the Card. Controls you nest\ninside keep their own disabled state. Required and invalid state belong on `CheckboxGroup` or\n`RadioGroup`, and so does radio read-only state."},"225":{"id":"/docs/components/checkbox","page_id":"/docs/components/checkbox","type":"page","content":"Checkbox","breadcrumbs":["Docs","Components"],"tags":[],"url":"/docs/components/checkbox"},"226":{"id":"/docs/components/checkbox-0","page_id":"/docs/components/checkbox","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/checkbox","content":"Accessible checkbox component for multi-select options with support for indeterminate states, validation, keyboard navigation, and flexible group layouts."},"227":{"id":"/docs/components/checkbox-1","page_id":"/docs/components/checkbox","type