rop)."],[633,"`focusable=\"false\"`: Prevents keyboard focus"],[2033,"`Grid` is a two-dimensional CSS Grid layout component for complex grid-based layouts. It extends `Box`, inheriting all `Box` capabilities (padding, elevation, rounding, self-alignment, and polymorphic `as` prop)."],[514,"`Heading` renders a semantic `h1`-`h6` element via the `level` prop.\nInside a `Modal`/`Dialog`, add `slot=\"title\"` and it labels the dialog automatically."],[223,"`href` renders the Card itself as a native link, named by its content unless you pass\n`aria-label`. A link Card cannot contain controls, so do not put CornerActions, buttons,\ninputs, or selection in an `href` Card. Clicking body text on an `onPress` or\nselection Card activates it; dragging that text selects it."],[212,"`href` renders the Card itself as a native link, so layered content like an elevated Box stays\nclickable. The link takes its name from its content unless you pass `aria-label`. Do not nest\ncontrols in a link Card."],[716,"`InlineDrawerPanel` is the collapsible content for the accordion pattern — a thin wrapper over RAC `DisclosurePanel` that hides when collapsed. The trigger is any component you slot in with `slot=\"trigger\"` — there's no dedicated trigger component."],[699,"`Input` is the single-line control inside a field, not a field on its own. Prefer `TextField` or `NumberField` as the parent; see those components for fuller examples."],[217,"`isDisabled` disables the Card's primary action or selection and fades the whole Card. A\ndisabled CheckboxGroup or RadioGroup does the same. Read-only selection keeps its value visible."],[224,"`isDisabled` disables the primary action or selection and fades the Card. Controls you nest\ninside keep their own disabled state. Required and invalid state belong on `CheckboxGroup` or\n`RadioGroup`, and so does radio read-only state."],[1909,"`legendPosition` puts the legend above or below the plot, or hides it with `null`. Multi-series charts get a bottom legend by default."],[515,"`level` sets the semantics and `size` sets the look, so the two never have to match. Without\n`size`, a heading takes the size scope's heading tier at any level."],[1964,"`lg` - Large spacing"],[766,"`ListBox` requires either `aria-label` or `aria-labelledby`. For a labeled, popover-style picker, prefer `Select`."],[1963,"`md` - Medium spacing"],[801,"`MenuTrigger` exposes its open state via `isOpen`/`onOpenChange`,\nwhich can be used to drive the rotation of a chevron icon."],[151,"`minValue` / `maxValue` bounds and `isDateUnavailable` per-day disabling"],[421,"`minValue` / `maxValue` bounds and `isDateUnavailable` per-day disabling"],[870,"`Modal` accepts `isOpen` and `onOpenChange` directly, so it can be controlled without a\n`ModalTrigger`. Useful when the modal is opened from several places at once."],[865,"`ModalTrigger` wraps a trigger button and a `<Modal>`, handling open state automatically. Based on RAC `DialogTrigger`."],[214,"`onPress` is the Card primary. Nested buttons keep their own hits, so Save does not open the\nModal. Compose a Card inside the Modal when the action is a focused form."],[1040,"`orientation` switches between `horizontal` (accent bar on top) and `vertical` (accent bar on the leading edge)."],[1761,"`orientation=\"horizontal\"` swaps the axes: categories run down the side and values across the bottom. Reach for it when the labels are long or the chart is really a ranking."],[1437,"`overflowLabels` is optional and defaults to \"Previous tabs\" and \"Next tabs\". Provide localized labels when needed; they should describe the logical direction rather than physical directions like \"left\" or \"right\", as the component automatically handles RTL layouts."],[1701,"`overlay` elevation panel positioned relative to its trigger, with an optional arrow"],[736,"`placement` does not flip in RTL; the side is decided by document/flex order."],[719,"`placement` selects the collapse axis (`left`/`right` → width, `top`/`bottom` → height)"],[945,"`PopoverTrigger` wraps a trigger button and a `<Popover>`, handling open state and positioning automatically.\nBased on RAC `DialogTrigger`. To anchor a popover to an element it doesn't wrap, pass `triggerRef` instead."],[722,"`prefers-reduced-motion` support"],[979,"`Pressable` accepts the React Aria press props, including `onPress`, `onPressStart`, `onPressEnd`, `onPressUp`, and `onPressChange`."],[984,"`Pressable` automatically applies React Aria state attributes such as `[data-hovered]`, `[data-pressed]`, `[data-focus-visible]`, and `[data-disabled]` to the child. Ensure the child component styles these states appropriately if it overrides the default `Pressable` styles."],[1095,"`RadioGroup` is composed: write `Label`, a `Group` holding the `Radio` items, `Text slot=\"description\"`, and `FieldError`. The `Group` takes its axis, gap, and presentational role from the group's `orientation`, so a bare `<Group>` is all you need; pass your own `direction`/`gap` to lay the items out differently. Each `Radio` takes label text next to the indicator. `orientation` also sets keyboard-navigation direction and ARIA."],[1928,"`renderTooltip` example combining a pair of series. Each pair shares a `colorIndex`\n(solid actual + dashed forecast); hovering either line shows the percent change of\nthe forecast against the actual for that pair, wrapped in the default styled popover."],[1929,"`renderTooltip` example styled as a period-over-period comparison card. Paired series\n(solid current period + dashed previous period) share a `colorIndex`; hovering either\nline shows both dated values and the percent change, wrapped in the default popover."],[1927,"`renderTooltip` lets you render a fully custom tooltip and know which curve is\nhovered. Paired series share a `colorIndex`; hovering either line shows a\ntooltip specific to that line, wrapped in the default styled popover."],[879,"`role=\"dialog\"` is applied automatically by the underlying React Aria `Dialog`